{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Independent exact-final-SHA TSV audit: PASS\n\nImmutable BASE: d6669496cae441fc8381b5ee6de21a3993defd84\nCorrective authored revision: b493118a04cc1004b0b8b1a3f84d4b8fc5ea9c27\nExact merged FINAL: d8438d69fb7dc6c3c42fac272943909e2059f535\nFINAL parent: 898d3e8f7f7e4f000c0b183dcc4336d17a8fb03b\nReviewer session: splintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\n\nValidated receipt: 99 unique data rows, 10 tab-separated fields per row, exact stable-id coverage, 99/99 bloat PASS, and 99/99 semantic PASS. All blocks shrink (7,413 -> 2,298 words). Exact-scope, immutable Python AST/runtime, JS non-comment, directive/shebang, DCO/trailer/Change-Id, and diff-integrity checks pass. The corrected prose accurately assigns bounded response latency to preview_or_job, includes secret expressions, and reserves determinism for the scripted decision while stating escalation cannot alter the verdict.\n\nImmutable-base YAML disposition: unrelated commit 1e7d9dbf4d4e6 added exactly two code-review failover-overlay data entries before the correction. They are not among the 99 ticket-owned prose blocks. Removing those two exact additions restores byte-for-byte ordered BASE YAML data, and FINAL-parent-to-FINAL YAML data is byte-identical.\n\nReceipt SHA-256 (header + 99 rows + trailing newline): 02e52e307d43ea99e5d420c1055764fe8a5693b5e7e40634899afa22e8e45a49\n\n```tsv\nstable_id\tbefore_citation\tfinal_citation\tpreserved_contract_or_consumer\tdirectives_exact\tbefore_words\tfinal_words\treviewer_session\tsemantic_pass\tbloat_pass\ncriterion_preview.py::D:module@1-34\tBASE:criterion_preview.py:1-34\tFINAL:criterion_preview.py:1-7\tPASS: Preview a plan-review criterion against an isolated fixture. LLM criteria run a Pass-1 finder; DET criteria scan a disposable repository. Context-dependent container/G3/G4/ISF finders raise :class:`PreviewError`. :func:`preview_or_job` bounds response latency and preserves timed-out work for polling. Overlay authoring couples routing and activation atomically.\tPASS\t313\t47\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\ncriterion_preview.py::D:preview_criterion@96-106\tBASE:criterion_preview.py:96-106\tFINAL:criterion_preview.py:69-74\tPASS: Preview an existing or inline criterion. ``DET`` uses grounding; other tiers use Pass-1. Unknown or context-dependent criteria raise :class:`PreviewError`. Timeout classifies late work as no-fire but does not bound direct-call latency.\tPASS\t106\t32\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\ncriterion_preview.py::D:preview_or_job@192-196\tBASE:criterion_preview.py:192-196\tFINAL:criterion_preview.py:157-161\tPASS: Return an inline preview or a pollable background job. Success and preview errors map to 200 and 400. Timeout leaves the worker running and returns ``(202, {status: \"pending\", job_id})`` for :func:`poll_job`.\tPASS\t60\t32\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\ncriterion_preview.py::D:_run_inline_finder@318-320\tBASE:criterion_preview.py:318-320\tFINAL:criterion_preview.py:283-283\tPASS: Run an unsaved rubric through Pass-1 under its inline id, without a prompt file.\tPASS\t40\t14\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\ncriterion_preview.py::D:author_criterion@472-478\tBASE:criterion_preview.py:472-478\tFINAL:criterion_preview.py:435-439\tPASS: Write a dotted criterion's filesystem-safe rubric, then optionally activate it. Routing and activation share one atomic overlay update. Prompt-first failure leaves a harmless inactive rubric. Returns its path and propagates authoring errors.\tPASS\t78\t32\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\ncriterion_preview.py::D:write_criterion_overlay@491-497\tBASE:criterion_preview.py:491-497\tFINAL:criterion_preview.py:452-456\tPASS: Atomically update a criterion's routing and activation membership. Failure leaves the previously written rubric inactive. Callers must then invalidate the registry caches.\tPASS\t70\t22\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\ncriterion_preview.py::D:author_criterion_overlay@541-555\tBASE:criterion_preview.py:541-555\tFINAL:criterion_preview.py:498-503\tPASS: Activate an explicit dotted criterion id and refresh the registry caches. The logical id is never recovered from its one-way filename mapping. Validation re-resolves the merged registry; failure restores the prior overlay and leaves the prompt inactive.\tPASS\t141\t37\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\ncriterion_preview.py::C:preview_criterion@107-109\tBASE:criterion_preview.py:107-109\tFINAL:criterion_preview.py:75-76\tPASS: # Executor shutdown can wait for a timed-out worker. preview_or_job owns bounded # response latency and retains that worker for polling.\tPASS\t42\t19\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\ncriterion_preview.py::C:module@162-166\tBASE:criterion_preview.py:162-166\tFINAL:criterion_preview.py:129-131\tPASS: # ── Synchronous within the timeout; otherwise return a pollable job. ────────────── # The locked, process-local store replaces pending entries with terminal results. # Short-lived single-user sessions make durability and eviction unnecessary here.\tPASS\t58\t28\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\ncriterion_preview.py::C:write_criterion_overlay@509-512\tBASE:criterion_preview.py:509-512\tFINAL:criterion_preview.py:468-469\tPASS: # ``gate`` selects the overlay section and activation only; it is not persisted in # the entry. Missing or unknown values retain the plan_review default.\tPASS\t45\t23\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\neditor_assets/src/configValidation.js::J@1-18\tBASE:editor_assets/src/configValidation.js:1-18\tFINAL:editor_assets/src/configValidation.js:1-5\tPASS: /** * Validate rebar config before Save. Valid responses enable Save; errors and unavailable * responses remain visibly distinct and fail closed. Requests are debounced, and per-kind * help comes from the server-backed REBAR_KIND_HELP registry. */\tPASS\t148\t31\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\neditor_assets/src/index.js::J@1-22\tBASE:editor_assets/src/index.js:1-22\tFINAL:editor_assets/src/index.js:1-5\tPASS: /** * Browser workflow editor. It auto-lays out BPMN, exposes typed rebar properties, and * preserves extension data through Save's token-authenticated BPMN-to-IR round trip. * The host injects REBAR_DIAGRAM, REBAR_TOKEN, and REBAR_MODDLE. */\tPASS\t180\t28\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\neditor_assets/src/insertionProvider.js::J@1-19\tBASE:editor_assets/src/insertionProvider.js:1-19\tFINAL:editor_assets/src/insertionProvider.js:1-5\tPASS: /** * Typed context-pad and palette insertion. The category-grouped chooser maps scripted * ops to named ScriptTasks (`uses:`) and prompts to named ServiceTasks (`prompt:`), so * both round-trip through the IR. Canvas entries open the side-panel chooser. */\tPASS\t167\t33\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\neditor_assets/src/insertionProvider.js::J@34-37\tBASE:editor_assets/src/insertionProvider.js:34-37\tFINAL:editor_assets/src/insertionProvider.js:20-21\tPASS: // Leaf kinds round-trip through NAME == action. Structural kinds are completed in the // panel; batch starts as a ServiceTask with a recognizable rebar:Config seed.\tPASS\t62\t24\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\neditor_assets/src/insertionProvider.js::J@51-54\tBASE:editor_assets/src/insertionProvider.js:51-54\tFINAL:editor_assets/src/insertionProvider.js:35-36\tPASS: // Insert on the root, seed structural config, and select the new step so its typed // editor opens immediately. Used by the side panel and E2E harness.\tPASS\t56\t26\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\neditor_assets/src/promptLibrary.js::J@1-17\tBASE:editor_assets/src/promptLibrary.js:1-17\tFINAL:editor_assets/src/promptLibrary.js:1-5\tPASS: /** * Token-authenticated prompt library, typed insertion chooser, and create/edit panel. * It groups built-in and project entries, previews write targets, surfaces server errors, * validates ids, and confirms before discarding unsaved edits. */\tPASS\t138\t30\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\neditor_assets/src/promptLibrary.js::J@43-45\tBASE:editor_assets/src/promptLibrary.js:43-45\tFINAL:editor_assets/src/promptLibrary.js:31-32\tPASS: // REBAR_CONTRACTS mixes ops and prompts; treat names absent from the prompt catalog as // scripted ops.\tPASS\t44\t15\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\neditor_assets/src/promptLibrary.js::J@69-72\tBASE:editor_assets/src/promptLibrary.js:69-72\tFINAL:editor_assets/src/promptLibrary.js:56-57\tPASS: // The on-demand chooser asks only leaf kinds for an action. NAMELESS_KINDS hides that // choice for structural steps, whose config is completed after insertion.\tPASS\t50\t23\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\neditor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx::J@1-20\tBASE:editor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx:1-20\tFINAL:editor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx:1-5\tPASS: /** * Typed Rebar property editor for semantic BPMN elements. Each control mutates one slice * of the shared rebar:Config blob, so unknown keys survive round trips. There is no raw * JSON editor; invalid field values show errors without replacing prior data. */\tPASS\t229\t40\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\neditor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx::J@94-96\tBASE:editor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx:94-96\tFINAL:editor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx:79-80\tPASS: // Parse empty or malformed rebar:Config as {} for safe st