ng; each field feeds /library/create routing. // fail_mode and detector apply only to DET entries.\tPASS\t37\t22\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\neditor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx::J@1160-1166\tBASE:editor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx:1160-1166\tFINAL:editor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx:1089-1091\tPASS: // Build routing only for genuine criterion activation. A batch criterion's referenced // prompt is not an overlay id, so its picker returns null instead of forcing project.* // validation and stranding the step reference.\tPASS\t77\t32\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\neditor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx::J@1584-1587\tBASE:editor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx:1584-1587\tFINAL:editor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx:1509-1510\tPASS: // Close forms opened for another element so module-global state cannot target this // element's remembered criterion index.\tPASS\t54\t16\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\neditor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx::J@1821-1826\tBASE:editor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx:1821-1826\tFINAL:editor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx:1744-1746\tPASS: // ─── Read-only Effective Policy provenance ───────────────────────────────────── // Render the compiled projection separately from authored controls, with no write path. // Unavailable payloads show the compiler's located remedy.\tPASS\t75\t23\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\neditor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx::J@1917-1919\tBASE:editor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx:1917-1919\tFINAL:editor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx:1837-1838\tPASS: // Branch editing covers only structured `when`; other keys survive the slice write // while arm and connection authoring remains deferred.\tPASS\t39\t19\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\neditor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx::J@1948-1950\tBASE:editor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx:1948-1950\tFINAL:editor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx:1867-1867\tPASS: // Keep read-only compiled policy provenance separate from authored workflow controls.\tPASS\t32\t10\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\neditor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx::J@1963-1966\tBASE:editor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx:1963-1966\tFINAL:editor_assets/src/rebarProvider.jsx:1880-1881\tPASS: // Render authoring forms for batch criteria, agent prompt/if pickers, and scripted // if pickers—the entry points that can create their referenced records.\tPASS\t46\t23\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nexamples/review_skeleton.yaml::Y@2-12\tBASE:examples/review_skeleton.yaml:2-12\tFINAL:examples/review_skeleton.yaml:1-5\tPASS: # yaml-language-server: $schema=https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/schemas/workflow.v3.schema.json # # Retained offline visual-editing sample for the v3 four-pass review shape: precompute # overlays, batch prompt-backed criteria, aggregate verification, then deterministic # decision. Real gates live under workflow/gates/.\tPASS\t102\t38\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nexamples/review_skeleton.yaml::Y@31-33\tBASE:examples/review_skeleton.yaml:31-33\tFINAL:examples/review_skeleton.yaml:24-25\tPASS: # 2. Run prompt-backed Pass-1 criteria in budgeted batches; include `security` only # when its overlay trigger is true.\tPASS\t33\t17\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nexamples/review_skeleton.yaml::Y@44-46\tBASE:examples/review_skeleton.yaml:44-46\tFINAL:examples/review_skeleton.yaml:36-37\tPASS: # Use model classes: literal `claude-*` ids infer Anthropic and would pin the # example to the wrong provider.\tPASS\t38\t17\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nexecutor.py::D:module@1-32\tBASE:executor.py:1-32\tFINAL:executor.py:1-10\tPASS: Synchronous topological workflow execution. Scripted and agentic steps use injected seams while immutable :class:`RunState` threads named outputs. A tripwire forbids scheduler and retry imports. Adopt Burr only for: 1. durable cross-process pause/resume; 2. data-dependent non-linear flow; 3. required parallel step execution; or 4. Burr telemetry/UI as a product surface. The :class:`RunRecorder` seam supplies persistence, determinism, and idempotency.\tPASS\t248\t61\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nexecutor.py::D:new_run_id@83-89\tBASE:executor.py:83-89\tFINAL:executor.py:61-64\tPASS: Return a sortable, globally unique ``{ns-timestamp}-{uuid4hex}`` run id. It is generated once and persisted on every run and step event.\tPASS\t50\t21\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nexecutor.py::D:_capture_nondeterminism@94-106\tBASE:executor.py:94-106\tFINAL:executor.py:69-73\tPASS: Capture the engine clock, UUID, and seed once per step execution. Persisted values replay through ``ctx.captured``. A pre-marker crash may re-execute and recapture; effect safety remains the step's idempotency contract.\tPASS\t125\t31\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nexecutor.py::D:register_step@176-182\tBASE:executor.py:176-182\tFINAL:executor.py:137-140\tPASS: Register a scripted step and expose supplied contract metadata. The editor and reference linter consume the resulting :class:`StepContract`.\tPASS\t50\t19\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nexecutor.py::D:RunState@215-220\tBASE:executor.py:215-220\tFINAL:executor.py:170-170\tPASS: Immutable workflow inputs and completed outputs; updates return a new state.\tPASS\t42\t11\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nexecutor.py::D:resolve_value@284-289\tBASE:executor.py:284-289\tFINAL:executor.py:234-237\tPASS: Recursively resolve step/input, secret, and environment expressions in ``value``. A whole-string expression preserves its raw type; embedded values become text.\tPASS\t44\t21\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nexecutor.py::D:_resolve_terminal_output@345-348\tBASE:executor.py:345-348\tFINAL:executor.py:291-294\tPASS: Return the executed terminal leaf output, recursively following taken branches. Non-branch terminals retain their own output; nested results use full frame keys.\tPASS\t47\t22\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nexecutor.py::D:run_workflow@378-390\tBASE:executor.py:378-390\tFINAL:executor.py:324-329\tPASS: Validate, lint, and synchronously execute ``doc`` to its terminal output. Steps resolve expressions and thread named outputs; failure stops the run. A fresh id is used by default. ``target_ticket`` selects durable ticket recording when no recorder is supplied; otherwise state remains in memory.\tPASS\t94\t43\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nexecutor.py::D:sweep_orphan_snapshots@580-584\tBASE:executor.py:580-584\tFINAL:executor.py:499-502\tPASS: Best-effort removal of snapshot directories older than ``ttl_seconds``. Returns removed paths, skips failures, and is safe to repeat before each run.\tPASS\t42\t21\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nexecutor.py::C:StepContext@134-138\tBASE:executor.py:134-138\tFINAL:executor.py:101-102\tPASS: # Full execution frame key. Side effects use ``(run_id, frame_key)`` so nested # iterations remain distinct and replay-stable.\tPASS\t57\t16\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nexecutor.py::C:StepContext@143-147\tBASE:executor.py:143-147\tFINAL:executor.py:107-108\tPASS: # Persisted clock, UUID, and seed for this execution; status/result reads replay # these values instead of consulting live sources.\tPASS\t54\t19\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nexecutor.py::C:module@197-204\tBASE:executor.py:197-204\tFINAL:executor.py:155-159\tPASS: # Runner seams live in runners.py, remain re-exported here, and are constructed per run. # ── Recorder seam ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── # Recorder classes live in recorder.py but remain re-exported for compatibility.\tPASS\t53\t27\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nexecutor.py::C:module@337-341\tBASE:executor.py:337-341\tFINAL:executor.py:285-287\tPASS: # ── v2 worklist interpreter ────────────────────────────────────────────────── # Recursive frame execution lives in interpreter and is imported lazily to avoid # cycling back to this module's step interfaces. The Burr tripwire scans both files.\tPASS\t45\t28\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nexecutor.py::C:run_workflow@402-405\tBASE:executor.py:402-405\tFINAL:executor.py:341-341\tPASS: # Fill only missing inputs from declared defaults; explicit falsy values still win.\tPASS\t47\t12\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nexecutor.py::C:run_workflow@426-431\tBASE:executor.py:426-431\tFINAL:executor.py:362-363\tPASS: # Walk v2 frames. Leaf-only workflows retain v1 bare step keys and compatible # markers/results. The lazy import avoids cycling through the step interfaces.\tPASS\t63\t23\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nexecutor.py::C:run_workflow@450-454\tBASE:executor.py:450-454\tFINAL:executor.py:382-383\tPASS: # A terminal branch returns routing metadata, so follow its taken arm to the verdict; # plain terminals keep their own output.\tPASS\t62\t20\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nexecutor.py::C:_dispatch@491-495\tBASE:executor.py:491-495\tFINAL:executor.py:420-421\tPASS: # Add schema defaults beneath sparse runner output so downstream references remain # resolvable; explicit runner values always win.\tPASS\t55\t17\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nexecutor.py::C:_dispatch@507-512\tBASE:executor.py:507-512\tFINAL:executor.py:433-434\tPASS: # Offline/canned runners omit conditional provider_provenance. Supply None so gate # wiring resolves it and downstream verdicts still represent the record as absent.\tPASS\t70\t22\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nexecutor.py::C:module@561-566\tBASE:executor.py:561-566\tFINAL:executor.py:483-485\tPASS: # ── Snapshot TTL sweep ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── # Runs normally tear down snapshots; this lifecycle backstop removes crash orphans.\tPASS\t60\t14\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\ngates/code-review.yaml::Y@2-15\tBASE:gates/code-review.yaml:2-15\tFINAL:gates/code-review.yaml:1-6\tPASS: # yaml-language-server: $schema=https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/schemas/workflow.v3.schema.json # # Four-pass code review: recall can escalate from base to overlays; the scripted decision # remains deterministic, and escalation cannot change its verdict. `union.cap` sets the # escalation limit; criteria routing owns thresholds and posture. Topology runs assemble, # trigger, two recall rounds, merge, verify, decide, then coach.\tPASS\t125\t57\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\ngates/code-review.yaml::Y@98-102\tBASE:gates/code-review.yaml:98-102\tFINAL:gates/code-review.yaml:89-90\tPASS: # Pass-1 model belongs inside `batch:`; the interpreter ignores a step-level value. # Keep one rung so every criterion in the pass resolves deterministically.\tPASS\t57\t22\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\ngates/code-review.yaml::Y@138-142\tBASE:gates/code-review.yaml:138-142\tFINAL:gates/code-review.yaml:127-128\tPASS: # Pass-1 model belongs inside `batch:`; the interpreter ignores a step-level value. # Keep one rung so every criterion in the pass resolves deterministically.\tPASS\t57\t22\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\ngates/code-review.yaml::Y@184-191\tBASE:gates/code-review.yaml:184-191\tFINAL:gates/code-review.yaml:171-172\tPASS: # Pin Pass-2 to the configurable `standard` class. This avoids frontier fallback, # preserves deterministic temperature handling, and lets operators retarget the class.\tPASS\t106\t21\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\ngates/code-review.yaml::Y@244-251\tBASE:gates/code-review.yaml:244-251\tFINAL:gates/code-review.yaml:225-226\tPASS: # Carry the verify runner's stamped provider provenance verbatim. Recomputing can # diverge from the call that ran; a scripted source would always yield None.\tPASS\t94\t23\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\ngates/plan-review.yaml::Y@67-74\tBASE:gates/plan-review.yaml:67-74\tFINAL:gates/plan-review.yaml:67-68\tPASS: # Pass-1 uses frontier because it generates blocking findings; verify and coach use # standard. Consumers read only rung 0—context escalation uses sizing.MODEL_LADDER.\tPASS\t85\t23\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\ngates/plan-review.yaml::Y@171-176\tBASE:gates/plan-review.yaml:171-176\tFINAL:gates/plan-review.yaml:165-166\tPASS: # Branch on code_grounded to select agentic or single-turn verification. Decide and # coach stay inside each arm because frame-scoped references cannot reach nested siblings.\tPASS\t82\t23\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\ngates/plan-review.yaml::Y@198-201\tBASE:gates/plan-review.yaml:198-201\tFINAL:gates/plan-review.yaml:188-189\tPASS: # Scale the agentic verifier's step budget with findings, never below the # configured floor. `with:` is the v3 step's extension point.\tPASS\t54\t20\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\ngates/plan-review.yaml::Y@203-211\tBASE:gates/plan-review.yaml:203-211\tFINAL:gates/plan-review.yaml:191-193\tPASS: # Use the resolved model's maximum output budget to prevent truncation-driven # INDETERMINATE results. Per-finding scaling remains an additional floor for # models absent from the capacity table.\tPASS\t96\t25\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\ngates/plan-review.yaml::Y@242-245\tBASE:gates/plan-review.yaml:242-245\tFINAL:gates/plan-review.yaml:224-225\tPASS: # Coach blocking or surviving advisory findings. A clean pass skips the LLM call # and renders empty notes.\tPASS\t48\t17\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\ngates/plan-review.yaml::Y@282-288\tBASE:gates/plan-review.yaml:282-288\tFINAL:gates/plan-review.yaml:262-263\tPASS: # Carry the verify runner's provider provenance; recomputation can diverge # from the call that ran. Every coach arm must preserve it.\tPASS\t78\t20\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\ngates/plan-review.yaml::Y@308-314\tBASE:gates/plan-review.yaml:308-314\tFINAL:gates/plan-review.yaml:283-284\tPASS: # Carry the verify runner's provider provenance; recomputation can diverge # from the call that ran. Every coach arm must preserve it.\tPASS\t78\t20\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\ngates/plan-review.yaml::Y@363-366\tBASE:gates/plan-review.yaml:363-366\tFINAL:gates/plan-review.yaml:333-334\tPASS: # Coach blocking or surviving advisory findings. A clean pass skips the LLM call # and renders empty notes.\tPASS\t48\t17\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\ngates/plan-review.yaml::Y@403-409\tBASE:gates/plan-review.yaml:403-409\tFINAL:gates/plan-review.yaml:371-372\tPASS: # Carry the verify runner's provider provenance; recomputation can diverge # from the call that ran. Every coach arm must preserve it.\tPASS\t78\t20\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\ngates/plan-review.yaml::Y@429-435\tBASE:gates/plan-review.yaml:429-435\tFINAL:gates/plan-review.yaml:392-393\tPASS: # Carry the verify runner's provider provenance; recomputation can diverge # from the call that ran. Every coach arm must preserve it.\tPASS\t78\t20\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nplan_review_recovery.py::D:module@1-22\tBASE:plan_review_recovery.py:1-22\tFINAL:plan_review_recovery.py:1-6\tPASS: Reconstruct plan-review verdicts and metrics from gate run records. This strict leaf keeps rebar imports lazy and never imports ``gate_dispatch``, which re-exports these names for compatibility. Orchestrator attribute access is intentional: binding bare functions would defeat lifecycle monkeypatches.\tPASS\t193\t38\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nplan_review_recovery.py::D:GateContractError@56-59\tBASE:plan_review_recovery.py:56-59\tFINAL:plan_review_recovery.py:36-36\tPASS: The loaded gate lacks a step id required by recovery or metrics reconstruction.\tPASS\t53\t13\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nplan_review_recovery.py::D:_validate_gate_step_ids@79-83\tBASE:plan_review_recovery.py:79-83\tFINAL:plan_review_recovery.py:56-56\tPASS: Reject a loaded gate missing any recovery step id before execution.\tPASS\t56\t11\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nplan_review_recovery.py::D:_attach_plan_review_metrics@101-129\tBASE:plan_review_recovery.py:101-129\tFINAL:plan_review_recovery.py:74-79\tPASS: Attach recorder-derived plan-review timing, call-count, and usage metrics. ``det_ms`` covers precheck, ``llm_ms`` covers agent/batch steps, and ``total_ms`` also includes scripted overhead. Batch usage supplies token totals, raw records, and per-criterion data. Existing coverage survives partial or untimed records.\tPASS\t215\t39\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nplan_review_recovery.py::D:_attach_discovery_trace@195-199\tBASE:plan_review_recovery.py:195-199\tFINAL:plan_review_recovery.py:145-148\tPASS: Expose the batch discovery journal for sidecar retry evidence. The reducer ignores it, and surfaced output strips it after sidecar persistence.\tPASS\t56\t21\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nplan_review_recovery.py::D:strip_surfaced_journal@217-220\tBASE:plan_review_recovery.py:217-220\tFINAL:plan_review_recovery.py:166-166\tPASS: Remove persisted retry-journal keys before surfacing a verdict; tolerate non-dicts.\tPASS\t44\t10\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nplan_review_recovery.py::D:_attach_read_set@227-239\tBASE:plan_review_recovery.py:227-239\tFINAL:plan_review_recovery.py:173-177\tPASS: Record normalized repository paths observed across successful LLM steps. Set ``read_set_recorded`` only after a real fetch; absent telemetry must retain the fail-safe whole-HEAD fallback rather than masquerade as an empty read set.\tPASS\t141\t32\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nplan_review_recovery.py::D:_recover_plan_review_coach_failure@268-271\tBASE:plan_review_recovery.py:268-271\tFINAL:plan_review_recovery.py:206-209\tPASS: Recover a decided verdict from a coach-only failure, with empty coaching. Return ``None`` when decision also failed so the caller degrades to INDETERMINATE.\tPASS\t48\t23\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nplan_review_recovery.py::D:_recover_plan_review_verify_failure@323-328\tBASE:plan_review_recovery.py:323-328\tFINAL:plan_review_recovery.py:260-264\tPASS: Recover finder results after verification or decision fails. Preserve findings as unverified INDETERMINATE with ``verify_failed``; blocking-enabled findings still fail closed. Return ``None`` if finders also failed.\tPASS\t70\t26\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nplan_review_recovery.py::D:_cancelled_plan_review_verdict@480-485\tBASE:plan_review_recovery.py:480-485\tFINAL:plan_review_recovery.py:409-413\tPASS: Build an unsigned, sidecar-free INDETERMINATE for a stale mid-run cancellation. It bypasses floors and signing; withholding the sidecar avoids advancing the revision pinned by the next review.\tPASS\t57\t27\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nplan_review_recovery.py::C:module@31-36\tBASE:plan_review_recovery.py:31-36\tFINAL:plan_review_recovery.py:15-16\tPASS: # Central step-id vocabulary for recovery and metrics. Validate it against the loaded gate # at dispatch so YAML drift fails loudly instead of silently degrading the verdict.\tPASS\t88\t26\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nplan_review_recovery.py::C:_recover_plan_review_coach_failure@307-309\tBASE:plan_review_recovery.py:307-309\tFINAL:plan_review_recovery.py:245-246\tPASS: # Verification succeeded, so preserve its runner-stamped provenance instead of # recomputing a provider that may not have served the call.\tPASS\t41\t19\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nplan_review_recovery.py::C:_recover_plan_review_verify_failure@350-354\tBASE:plan_review_recovery.py:350-354\tFINAL:plan_review_recovery.py:286-287\tPASS: # Send preserved findings through Pass-3 with empty verifications, reusing the kernel's # schema-valid indeterminate decision instead of inventing a partial shape.\tPASS\t55\t20\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nplan_review_recovery.py::C:_recover_plan_review_verify_failure@380-383\tBASE:plan_review_recovery.py:380-383\tFINAL:plan_review_recovery.py:313-314\tPASS: # Verification produced no record, so omit provider_provenance; configuration cannot # truthfully identify a call that never completed.\tPASS\t45\t16\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\nplan_review_recovery.py::C:_degraded_plan_review_verdict@454-457\tBASE:plan_review_recovery.py:454-457\tFINAL:plan_review_recovery.py:385-386\tPASS: # Persist structured outage disposition when an error has an outcome, enabling retryable # exit 11. String-only failures remain plain INDETERMINATE.\tPASS\t46\t19\tsplintery-faulty-alleycat (b170-bdb6-1bc4-4c92)\tPASS\tPASS\n```"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789032496102614001,"uuid":"2f9ba6fc-fe40-43f0-81fa-357fcc7bbe67"}